WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.170
Choose this practice only where you are safe to pause.

2
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:12.135
Keep your eyes open, change position, or stop at any time.

3
00:00:13.835 --> 00:00:18.315
You do not need to bring a painful memory closer.

4
00:00:20.015 --> 00:00:29.400
If attention to grief feels too intense, return to the room, the ground, or an ordinary task.

5
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:36.125
Reaching out to someone you trust is also a valid next step.

6
00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:54.332
Begin with what supports you physically.

7
00:00:56.032 --> 00:01:00.747
Feel the floor, the chair, the bed, or the wall.

8
00:01:02.447 --> 00:01:12.387
Notice the clearest edge of your body: the feet inside socks, a hand resting on fabric, or the back meeting a surface.

9
00:01:35.918 --> 00:01:40.383
Look around slowly, if your eyes are open.

10
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:46.123
Let them rest on something plain and steady.

11
00:01:47.823 --> 00:01:51.673
A corner, a color, a line of light.

12
00:01:53.373 --> 00:01:57.273
You are here, in this room, at this time.

13
00:02:20.804 --> 00:02:32.384
Grief can appear as sadness, numbness, anger, love, tiredness, relief, confusion, or nothing that has a name.

14
00:02:34.084 --> 00:02:36.204
There is no correct feeling to find.

15
00:02:37.904 --> 00:02:43.379
Notice only what is already present and manageable enough to meet.

16
00:03:11.616 --> 00:03:22.741
If there is a body sensation connected with this moment, locate its edges rather than entering its center.

17
00:03:24.441 --> 00:03:33.111
Perhaps tightness in the throat, weight behind the eyes, hollowness in the chest, or heaviness in the arms.

18
00:03:34.811 --> 00:03:41.511
Let the sensation be one part of a larger body that is also touching support.

19
00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:18.715
Move attention between that sensation and a more neutral place.

20
00:04:20.415 --> 00:04:21.975
Grief for one breath.

21
00:04:23.675 --> 00:04:25.635
Feet for one breath.

22
00:04:27.335 --> 00:04:31.260
Grief, if it is workable.

23
00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.400
The support beneath you.

24
00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.980
You decide how close to come.

25
00:05:17.198 --> 00:05:21.943
Now notice the breath without using it to push anything away.

26
00:05:23.643 --> 00:05:25.203
The inhale may be shallow.

27
00:05:26.903 --> 00:05:28.543
The exhale may catch.

28
00:05:30.243 --> 00:05:35.943
Breathing does not have to become calm for this practice to be valid.

29
00:06:07.318 --> 00:06:11.473
You might silently say, this matters to me.

30
00:06:13.173 --> 00:06:16.343
Or, this is hard to carry.

31
00:06:18.043 --> 00:06:22.783
Choose words that are true without making the moment larger.

32
00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:31.143
If no words fit, let the hand rest somewhere that feels steady and say nothing.

33
00:07:02.517 --> 00:07:14.217
Grief often holds a bond: to a person, a place, a possibility, a time, or a part of life that changed.

34
00:07:15.917 --> 00:07:20.267
You do not need to explain that bond.

35
00:07:21.967 --> 00:07:31.067
For one moment, acknowledge that caring and loss can stand near each other.

36
00:08:10.285 --> 00:08:16.625
If an image or memory arrives, notice that it has arrived.

37
00:08:18.325 --> 00:08:20.005
You may let it pass.

38
00:08:21.705 --> 00:08:29.895
You may return to the color in the room, the pressure under your body, or the sound farthest away.

39
00:08:31.595 --> 00:08:35.965
Protecting your limits is part of this practice.

40
00:09:15.183 --> 00:09:18.023
Offer yourself one modest phrase.

41
00:09:19.723 --> 00:09:23.848
May I have room to breathe around this.

42
00:09:25.548 --> 00:09:29.388
May I move at the pace I can manage.

43
00:09:31.088 --> 00:09:35.413
May I accept support when it is available.

44
00:09:37.113 --> 00:09:47.453
If these words feel too warm or distant, use something simpler: one moment at a time.

45
00:10:34.515 --> 00:10:39.445
Feel the whole body now, not only the place that hurts.

46
00:10:41.145 --> 00:10:48.625
Notice temperature, clothing, contact, sound, and space.

47
00:10:50.325 --> 00:10:52.445
The difficult feeling may remain.

48
00:10:54.145 --> 00:10:58.370
It is not the only fact in the room.

49
00:11:37.588 --> 00:11:42.878
Consider what would be kind and practical after this practice.

50
00:11:44.578 --> 00:11:45.458
Water.

51
00:11:47.158 --> 00:11:47.758
Light.

52
00:11:49.458 --> 00:11:50.458
A blanket.

53
00:11:52.158 --> 00:11:53.118
Fresh air.

54
00:11:54.818 --> 00:11:56.578
A message to someone.

55
00:11:58.278 --> 00:11:59.718
A familiar routine.

56
00:12:01.418 --> 00:12:03.538
Or simply continuing slowly.

57
00:12:05.238 --> 00:12:11.378
You do not need to choose yet; notice which possibility feels least demanding.

58
00:12:42.752 --> 00:12:52.952
Notice whether any part of you is asking to be understood, and whether another part simply needs quiet.

59
00:12:54.652 --> 00:12:56.052
Both can be present.

60
00:12:57.752 --> 00:13:04.932
You do not have to make a story from the feeling or find a lesson inside it.

61
00:13:06.632 --> 00:13:17.597
For now, the task is smaller: remain in contact with one support, one breath, and the room that is holding this moment with you.

62
00:13:52.109 --> 00:13:54.309
Begin to orient outward.

63
00:13:56.009 --> 00:14:00.769
Let your eyes move and your head turn if that is comfortable.

64
00:14:02.469 --> 00:14:06.224
Feel the length of the arms and legs.

65
00:14:07.924 --> 00:14:12.564
Press gently into the surface beneath you and release.

66
00:14:36.095 --> 00:14:42.635
There is no finish line for grief, and this practice is not a treatment.

67
00:14:44.335 --> 00:14:52.635
It is one careful interval in which you did not have to carry the whole experience at once.

68
00:14:55.035 --> 00:15:00.000
Take the time you need before standing or moving on.
